-- Q611: Financial Statement Analysis [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The company is collecting receivables faster than in prior years","The company''s average collection period has increased from approximately 30 days to approximately 46 days","Revenue has decreased significantly over the two-year period","The company switched from accrual basis to cash basis accounting"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Per AICPA ratio analysis principles, receivables turnover equals net credit sales divided by average receivables. A decline from 12x to 8x means days sales outstanding increased from approximately 30 days (365/12) to approximately 46 days (365/8), indicating slower collections and potential credit quality deterioration.
Wrong (A): A declining turnover ratio means slower collections, not faster.
Wrong (C): The stem states sales remained relatively flat, so revenue decline is not supported.
Wrong (D): A change in accounting basis would require disclosure and is not implied by a turnover ratio change alone.$EXPL$
