-- Q653: Risk Management and Economics [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The IRR ranking is correct because Beta''s 25% return exceeds Alpha''s 18%, making Beta superior regardless of investment size or scale","Both metrics always agree for mutually exclusive projects, so the conflicting data presented in this scenario is mathematically impossible","The NPV ranking is more reliable because Alpha''s $450,000 NPV creates $130,000 more shareholder value than Beta''s $320,000, and IRR ignores scale differences","Neither metric is useful because NPV and IRR are only valid for evaluating independent projects, not mutually exclusive alternatives"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 360-10-35, NPV is the more reliable criterion for mutually exclusive projects because it directly measures dollar increases in shareholder wealth. Alpha creates $450,000 vs. Beta''s $320,000. The conflict arises because IRR assumes reinvestment at the project''s own rate rather than WACC and ignores that 18% on $2M generates more absolute value than 25% on $1M.
Wrong (A): A higher percentage return does not compensate for smaller absolute value creation when projects are mutually exclusive.
Wrong (B): NPV-IRR conflicts are common with different project scales or timing patterns.
Wrong (D): Both metrics apply to mutually exclusive projects, though NPV is the superior decision criterion.$EXPL$
