  choices = $EXPL$["Total expense is $350,000 (10,000 x $35 intrinsic value) because ASC 718 requires mark-to-market adjustment for stock price changes","Total expense is $0 because stock options are not considered compensation until the options are actually exercised","Total expense is $450,000 (10,000 x $45 stock price) because the full stock price at grant date measures the compensation cost","Total expense is $120,000 (10,000 x $12 grant-date fair value) recognized over the vesting period, fixed at the grant date"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 718, compensation cost for equity-classified stock options is measured at the grant-date fair value ($12 per option via Black-Scholes) and is not remeasured for subsequent stock price changes. The total $120,000 is recognized over the vesting period. Subsequent appreciation benefits the employee but does not create additional expense.
