  choices = $EXPL$["At 80% ownership, only 80% of the unrealized profit ($12,000) is eliminated, while at 100% the full $15,000 is eliminated with NCI absorbing the difference","The full $15,000 is eliminated at both ownership levels because consolidated entities cannot report intercompany profit; NCI is unaffected because this is a downstream sale","No elimination is necessary at either ownership level because the subsidiary holds legal title making it a legitimate third-party transaction","At 80% ownership, the unrealized profit is $60,000 allocated between parent and NCI; at 100% the profit is zero because wholly-owned subsidiaries cannot transact"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 810-10-45-18, unrealized intercompany profit on unsold inventory must be fully eliminated regardless of ownership percentage. The unrealized profit is $15,000 (25% of $60,000 markup). Because this is a downstream sale, the full elimination is charged to the parent''s share and NCI is unaffected.
