-- Q694: Advanced Consolidations [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Kept at its original historical cost on the acquirer''s books with no adjustment required","Remeasured to acquisition-date fair value with any resulting gain or loss recognized in earnings","Written off entirely and removed from the acquirer''s financial statements at the acquisition date","Adjusted only for cumulative equity method income earned since the initial investment date"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 805-10-25-10, when control is obtained in a step acquisition, the previously held equity interest must be remeasured to acquisition-date fair value with any gain or loss recognized in earnings. This ensures the entire combination is measured at fair value on the control date.
