-- Q695: Advanced Consolidations [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["In both scenarios the $150,000 gain is eliminated and $30,000 excess depreciation reversed annually; downstream charges the parent while upstream allocates 20% to NCI","The upstream sale requires no consolidation adjustments because the parent receives an asset from a subsidiary it already controls","Downstream sales never require elimination because the parent is the controlling entity, while upstream sales require full elimination","The depreciation adjustment differs between directions because the asset''s useful life changes depending on the intercompany transfer direction"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 810-10-45, intercompany transactions must be fully eliminated regardless of direction. In both cases, the $150,000 gain is eliminated and $30,000 annual excess depreciation ($150,000 / 5 years) is reversed. The key distinction is NCI allocation: in a downstream sale the parent bears the full elimination, while in an upstream sale NCI absorbs its 20% share.
Wrong (B): All intercompany transactions require elimination in consolidation, regardless of transfer direction.
