WHERE id = 712;

-- Q713: Derivatives and Hedging [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The speculation exception for contracts entered into for investment or trading purposes","The normal purchases and normal sales scope exception under ASC 815-10-15-22","The embedded derivative exception for components within a non-derivative host contract","The de minimis exception for contracts below a specified notional amount threshold"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 815-10-15-22, the normal purchases and normal sales (NPNS) exception permits entities to exclude contracts for physical delivery of nonfinancial assets used in normal operations from derivative accounting. Bridgeport''s forward qualifies because it involves physical delivery of copper for regular production.
Wrong (A): There is no speculation exception; speculative derivatives must be accounted for under ASC 815.
Wrong (C): The embedded derivative exception addresses components within hybrid instruments, not standalone forward contracts.
Wrong (D): ASC 815 does not provide a de minimis exception based on notional amount thresholds.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 713;

-- Q719: Derivatives and Hedging [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Immediately reclassified to earnings in full upon discontinuance of the hedge designation","Left in OCI and reclassified to earnings when the hedged forecasted transaction affects earnings in future periods","Reversed against the hedging instrument''s carrying amount on the balance sheet at the discontinuance date","Written off directly to retained earnings as a prior-period adjustment upon hedge discontinuance"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 815-30-40-1, when cash flow hedge accounting is discontinued, cumulative gains or losses in AOCI remain and are reclassified to earnings when the forecasted transaction affects earnings. Immediate reclassification occurs only if the forecasted transaction is no longer probable.
Wrong (A): Amounts are not immediately reclassified unless the forecasted transaction is no longer probable of occurring.
Wrong (C): OCI balances are not reversed against the hedging instrument; they remain in AOCI for future reclassification.
Wrong (D): OCI amounts are reclassified through earnings, not written off directly to retained earnings.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 719;

-- Q721: State and Local Government Reporting [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Fund-level recognizes $3 million and government-wide recognizes $2.6 million, because fund statements use the full levy amount","Both recognize $3 million because the full levy is measurable and collection timing is irrelevant under both measurement bases","Fund-level recognizes $2.85 million (collected plus available within 60 days) while government-wide recognizes $3 million under full accrual","Fund-level recognizes $2.6 million on a cash basis while government-wide recognizes $2.85 million including the 60-day availability window"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under modified accrual (GASB fund-level), revenue must be measurable and available, typically collected within 60 days per GASB 33. The $2.6M collected plus $250,000 within 60 days totals $2.85M; the $150,000 expected in October is deferred. Under full accrual (government-wide per GASB 34), the full $3M is recognized at the levy date regardless of collection timing.
Wrong (A): This reverses the relationship; fund-level is more restrictive than government-wide, not less.
Wrong (B): Modified accrual explicitly requires availability, not just measurability.
Wrong (D): The 60-day availability window applies to fund-level modified accrual, not to government-wide full accrual.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 721;

-- Q723: State and Local Government Reporting [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Only governmental activities, excluding both business-type and fiduciary activities from reporting","Governmental and business-type activities, but not fiduciary activities held in trust for others","All fund types including fiduciary funds, because government-wide statements present the complete picture","Only business-type activities, because governmental activities are reported exclusively at the fund level"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under GASB 34, government-wide statements report governmental activities and business-type activities but exclude fiduciary activities. Fiduciary resources are held in trust for others and are not available for the government''s own programs, so they appear only in fund-level fiduciary statements.
Wrong (A): Government-wide statements include both governmental and business-type activities, not governmental alone.
Wrong (C): Fiduciary activities are excluded from government-wide statements and reported only at the fund level.
Wrong (D): Governmental activities are reported on both government-wide and fund-level statements.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 723;

-- Q724: State and Local Government Reporting [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Both statements report a $450,000 capital asset and depreciate it over its useful life under uniform GASB 34 treatment","Fund statements report a $450,000 expenditure reducing fund balance, while government-wide statements capitalize the asset and depreciate it over time","Fund statements capitalize the asset while government-wide statements expense it, because government-wide uses a shorter-term measurement focus","Both statements report a $450,000 expenditure because governments cannot capitalize assets under current GASB standards"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under GASB 34, governmental fund statements use the current financial resources measurement focus, so the $450,000 is an expenditure reducing fund balance immediately. Government-wide statements use the economic resources focus, so the asset is capitalized and depreciated over its useful life. This dual treatment serves different accountability objectives.
Wrong (A): GASB 34 preserved different treatments at the fund level versus government-wide level; they are not uniform.
Wrong (C): This reverses the treatment; fund statements expense while government-wide capitalize.
Wrong (D): GASB 34 requires capitalization of capital assets in government-wide statements.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 724;
